message: "If you use these data or this code, please cite them using the metadata below and the associated article."
type: software
title: "Data and code for: Linking fecal indicator limits to gastrointestinal illness risk for ritual bathing in the Ganga at Varanasi, India"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-05"
license: CC-BY-4.0
authors:
  - family-names: Tekile
    given-names: Ararso Beshea
    affiliation: "Department of Civil Engineering, Indian Institute of Technology (Banaras Hindu University), Varanasi, India"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # add your ORCID iD
  - family-names: Singh
    given-names: Prabhat Kumar
    affiliation: "Department of Civil Engineering, Indian Institute of Technology (Banaras Hindu University), Varanasi, India"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # add your ORCID iD
abstract: >-
  Fecal indicator counts (total coliforms, fecal coliforms, Escherichia coli, fecal streptococci and enterococci) in 44 water
  samples from four bathing sites at Varanasi, India (June 2025 to May 2026), and a self-contained Python notebook that
  recomputes the Public Health Risk Quotient (PHRQ), the quantitative microbial risk model for gastrointestinal illness per
  bathing event, the sensitivity analyses and the figures and tables of the associated article.
keywords:
  - Ganga River
  - bathing water
  - fecal indicator bacteria
  - quantitative microbial risk assessment
  - Public Health Risk Quotient
  - gastrointestinal illness
  - India
repository-code: "https://github.com/ArarsoBeshea/ganga-qmra"
